# 🔄 WEEK 2: COROUTINES & REPOSITORIES

## Day 8-9: Repository Pattern (SOLID)

### Learning: Single Responsibility Principle

**Bad (Violation):**
```kotlin
class UserViewModel {
    fun saveUser(user: User) {
        // Database logic here - WRONG!
        db.userDao().insert(user)
    }
}
```

**Good (SRP):**
```kotlin
// Repository handles data
class UserRepository {
    suspend fun saveUser(user: User) {
        dao.insert(user)
    }
}

// ViewModel handles UI logic
class UserViewModel(private val repository: UserRepository) {
    fun saveUser(user: User) = viewModelScope.launch {
        repository.saveUser(user)
    }
}
```

### Create Interface (Dependency Inversion):

```kotlin
interface UserRepository {
    suspend fun insertUser(user: User): Resource<Unit>
    suspend fun getUserById(id: String): Resource<User?>
    fun getAllUsersFlow(): Flow<Resource<List<User>>>
}

class UserRepositoryImpl(
    private val dao: UserDao
) : UserRepository {
    // Implementation
}
```

**SOLID Applied:**
- S: Single Responsibility (Repository only handles data)
- O: Open/Closed (Extend with new implementations)
- L: Liskov Substitution (Any UserRepository works)
- I: Interface Segregation (Focused interface)
- D: Dependency Inversion (Depend on abstraction)

